cff-version: 1.2.0
title: BarcalaReviewApp
message: >-
  If you use this software in a review, please cite it, and please also
  cite ASReview and the SAFE procedure where you used the active learning
  or the stopping rule.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Barcala
    given-names: Victoria
    affiliation: >-
      HU University of Applied Sciences Utrecht, Research Group Financial
      Inclusion and New Entrepreneurship
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   <- add yours
repository-code: "https://github.com/REPLACE-ME/BarcalaReviewApp"
abstract: >-
  A local screening workbench for systematic literature reviews. It merges
  exports from several bibliographic databases into one corpus that records
  where each record came from, prioritises title-and-abstract screening with
  active learning, applies a formal stopping rule, and generates the PRISMA
  2020 flow diagram from the decision records themselves rather than from
  figures entered by hand.
keywords:
  - systematic review
  - evidence synthesis
  - screening
  - active learning
  - PRISMA
  - bibliometrics
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-03"
